00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:40.000
Let's talk about HETE, Hyper Text Transfer Protocol.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:47.600
Before we jump into the nitty-gritty details of the protocol and how it works, it's important to understand why we should care.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:51.100
Let's talk about image sharing.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:58.800
So you've got your camera phone and you take a couple of pictures.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:04.200
Now, it's important to remember that 20 years ago, right, in the 90s and early 2000s,

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:09.700
it wasn't easy to share digital photos with a friend or family member.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:11.600
It was easy to take photos.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:17.600
We've had digital cameras for a long time, right, but it wasn't easy to share them.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:24.200
These days, if you use an app like Instagram, right, you take your photos and then I on my phone

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:31.200
can fairly seamlessly download your photos over the Internet onto my phone.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:36.800
And it's really important to understand that this is really the secret to Instagram success.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:43.200
They made photo sharing really, really easy and they did it just using the Internet.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.800
So you may be wondering what the heck does this have to do with HTTP?

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:53.400
Well, HTTP is the protocol that was almost certainly used to download those images.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:58.000
HTTP is the most popular protocol for communicating online.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:07.500
You've probably noticed that every time you go to a website, you see that HTTP colon slash slash section of the URL, right?

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:14.900
That's because every time you visit a website online, you're using the HTTP protocol to do it.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:22.500
So I've used this word protocol protocol a couple of times and you may be wondering what the heck is a protocol.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.600
Sounds like a really complex, really complex thing.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:26.500
It's actually not.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.500
Protocols are very simple.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:33.400
Let's jump right into what we mean when we say protocol.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:40.800
Let's imagine that I write a note to you just on a piece of paper that says raise.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:45.900
Raise your hand.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:50.000
I write this down on a piece of paper and I hand it to you.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.000
And when you get the piece of paper, you read it and you raise your hand.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:01.900
So the question is, upon reading the piece of paper, how did you know that I wanted you to raise your hand, right?

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:09.000
You saw these you saw these symbols on the piece of paper and somehow you were able to understand the hand should be raised.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:14.900
Well, it's because we have a protocol for communicating over text, right?

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:23.100
We've decided that these symbols that look like this are A-I-S-E that they form a word, right?

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:27.100
And that word means to lift something up and hand.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:33.300
We've decided that these symbols H-A-N-D mean, you know, this thing at the end of my arm.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:42.200
And it's just a set of rules that me as the person communicating and you as the person I'm communicating to have agreed upon.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:45.800
And now that we've agreed upon that set of rules, we can communicate, right?

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:49.400
Over this, in this case, the medium of a piece of paper.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:52.800
A protocol on the Internet works in the same way.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:56.000
We decide upon a set of rules, right?

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:01.600
And then two computers can both follow those rules and communicate with each other.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:05.300
In the case of computers, instead of sending plain text, right?

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:10.300
R-A-I-S-E, we would send kind of strings of ones and zeros.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:11.900
But the idea is the same.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:17.900
This is just information that's sent between two computers over a network and the protocol, right?

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:20.200
Hypertext transfer protocol.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:28.200
The protocol is what tells the computers how to parse this information as something useful.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:37.300
Because we have this protocol, this way of parsing the ones and zeros as useful information,

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:41.200
I am able to send you a photo over the Internet, right?

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:44.900
Again, it's just a bunch of ones and zeros that represent something.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:48.600
But because you and I agree on this protocol or this language,

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:53.300
I can send you the image of, for example, your niece's birthday party, right?

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:58.600
And your phone is able to parse all that information and display an image.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:01.900
But that's what makes HTTP so powerful.

