00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:40.700
All right, HTTP requests and responses.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:44.600
So at the heart of HTTP is a simple request-response system.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:47.100
The requesting computer, also known as the client,

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:50.500
here we have our client, asks another computer,

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:53.200
in this case the server, for some information.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:55.800
So when we make an HTTP request, right,

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:59.800
we, acting as the client, make a request to a server.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:02.000
The server processes that request

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:05.400
and sends some information back to us in a response.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:09.900
That's the entire HTTP life cycle.

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:11.800
It's all based on request-response.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:13.400
It's very synchronous in that way, right?

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:17.000
I send a request, then I have to sit and wait

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:20.500
till a response comes back, right?

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:23.100
And then those words, client and server,

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:26.300
it's important to just understand that when we say client,

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:28.400
we just mean the computer sending the request.

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.600
When we say server, we mean the computer

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.200
that's responding to the request.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.000
And that's really all it means.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.600
There's not like a special type of computer.

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:40.000
It's really just who's doing the sending

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:44.800
and who's doing the receiving in any given communication.

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:47.400
So we'll talk a little more about the specifics

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:49.400
of requests and responses later.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.100
For now, it's important to think of it

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:52.700
as a simple question-and-answer system.

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:54.900
So we're asking questions to the server

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:56.000
and we're getting answers, right?

