And as a general rule, it's important to understand

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:03.400
that generally speaking,

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:07.500
clients exist on the front end of an application

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:12.500
and servers exist on the backend of an application.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:18.200
The front end of an application is what the user sees.

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:21.600
So it's typically a mobile app or a website, right?

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:25.200
It's the thing that the user is directly interacting with.

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:27.700
The backend is essentially everything else.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.100
And in order to demonstrate that,

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:31.600
