Debuggers are optional.

01:59:53.600 --> 01:59:57.600
Debuggers are tools that we can use to help us debug our code.

01:59:57.600 --> 01:59:59.600
Some people like them.

01:59:59.600 --> 02:00:00.600
Some people don't.

02:00:00.600 --> 02:00:03.600
Some people use them for certain things or not for other things.

02:00:03.600 --> 02:00:06.600
If you've ever used a debugger, you'll know what I'm talking about.

02:00:06.600 --> 02:00:12.600
But basically a debugger is something that allows you to kind of step through your code one line at a time.

02:00:12.600 --> 02:00:19.600
So instead of running your entire program at once, you run it in debug mode, which allows you to kind of step through the program.

02:00:19.600 --> 02:00:21.600
Just one line of execution at a time.

02:00:21.600 --> 02:00:24.600
So you can see like what's going wrong.

02:00:24.600 --> 02:00:31.600
Where a more primitive form of debugging is to just add, you know, console dot log statements or print statements.

02:00:31.600 --> 02:00:37.600
So you can see what data is present in your application at which points.

02:00:37.600 --> 02:00:39.600
How you debug is up to you.

02:00:39.600 --> 02:00:41.600
Some people like debuggers.

02:00:41.600 --> 02:00:42.600
Some people don't.

02:00:42.600 --> 02:00:49.600
To be honest, I think it depends a lot on the kind of code you're working on as to whether you should use a debugger or not.

02:00:49.600 --> 02:00:53.600
But at the end of the day, they are not they're not required.

