We've got some information about each movie, right?

02:22:17.600 --> 02:22:22.600
It's ID, it's genre, it's title, director.

02:22:22.600 --> 02:22:28.600
So JSON data can really be structured in many different ways, right?

02:22:28.600 --> 02:22:30.600
We could have another key in here.

02:22:30.600 --> 02:22:35.600
We have movies in one array and we could have actors in another array under a different key.

02:22:35.600 --> 02:22:43.600
But the important point is that it's a very flexible way to kind of send structured data as plain text.

02:22:43.600 --> 02:22:46.600
So as developers, it's really simple to work with.

02:22:46.600 --> 02:22:55.600
We can take that plain text and parse it into our program and work with that data as just variables, right, within our program.

02:22:55.600 --> 02:23:06.600
So because JSON is plain text, if we're to bring that network response directly into our code and parse the response body,

02:23:06.600 --> 02:23:10.600
we would really just be looking at binary data that represents text.

02:23:10.600 --> 02:23:14.600
That's not super useful to us in our JavaScript code, right?

