03:11:53.600 --> 03:11:59.600
So HTTP put is by far the most common HTTP method for updating resources.

03:11:59.600 --> 03:12:03.600
However, patch is another one that is sometimes used.

03:12:03.600 --> 03:12:05.600
And here's the difference.

03:12:05.600 --> 03:12:15.600
The intended difference for these two HTTP methods was that put would swap out entire resources or update entire resources.

03:12:15.600 --> 03:12:20.600
Whereas patch would just update partial sections of a resource.

03:12:20.600 --> 03:12:23.600
So here's an example with the users that we just updated.

03:12:23.600 --> 03:12:30.600
We essentially put an ID in the URL path to indicate which user we wanted to update.

