And we said this is the new user object with all the properties update the whole thing.

03:12:38.600 --> 03:12:43.600
Right. So that's kind of the intended use case of a put a patch would have looked something like.

03:12:43.600 --> 03:12:46.600
Well, we still include that ID in the URL.

03:12:46.600 --> 03:12:50.600
But now instead of an entire user object, maybe we just have a name field.

03:12:50.600 --> 03:12:54.600
And we say we just want to swap out the name or we just want to update the name.

03:12:54.600 --> 03:12:57.600
Right. So that would be what patch was intended for.

03:12:57.600 --> 03:13:01.600
Now, in practice, you won't see patch used very often.

03:13:01.600 --> 03:13:08.600
Typically, servers just use put for all sorts of updates, whether it's partial or full.

